<title>UK: UK &quot;wise people&quot; see RPIX at 3.0 pct 1998.</title>
<headline>UK &quot;wise people&quot; see RPIX at 3.0 pct 1998.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's underlying inflation rate which excludes mortgage interest payments and is targetted by the government will stand at 3.0 percent in 1998, the report by the six member panel of independent forecasters published on Friday said.</p>
<p>The government's target range is one to four percent with a target of 2.5 percent by the middle of next year.</p>
<p>-- John Speck, London Newsroom +44 171 542-8663</p>
